      'zh-CN': '正解（＝用错的那句）：<b>「この へやは 広い 上に、家賃が 高い。」</b>。<b>「広い」是优点、「家賃が 高い」是缺点</b>，方向相反——<b>上に 前后必须同为优点或同为缺点</b>。<br>这句要说的其实是「虽然宽敞，但租金贵」，该用<b>〜が</b>／<b>〜けれど</b>／<b>〜かわりに</b>。<br>另外三句都同方向：2 两个优点、3 两个优点、4 两个倒霉事（迷路又下雨）。<br>解法：<b>先各自标上「好」或「坏」，一好一坏就直接排除</b>。',
      'en': 'Answer (the incorrect usage): <b>「この へやは 広い 上に、家賃が 高い。」</b>. <b>「広い」 is a plus and 「家賃が 高い」 is a minus</b>, so they point in opposite directions. <b>With 上に, both halves must be pluses or both must be minuses</b>.<br>What this sentence really means is “it\'s spacious, but the rent is high,” which calls for <b>〜が</b>／<b>〜けれど</b>／<b>〜かわりに</b>.<br>The other three all point the same way: option 2 has two pluses, option 3 has two pluses, and option 4 has two misfortunes (getting lost, then rain).<br>Approach: <b>label each half “good” or “bad”; if one is good and the other bad, rule it out at once</b>.',
